  Three things here are load-bearing:

  1. The word "unlimited" appears nowhere and must not. Vocele hard-stops at the plan allowance,
     and a suspension for volume fails the first condition of the ASA/FTC test for a lawful
     "unlimited" claim. Competitor Fluently wrote "there are no daily or monthly limits" INSIDE
     its Terms of Use — an FAQ pasted into a contract is an operative term, and the more specific
     one. Do not import that shape here.
  2. Section 5 is Speak's express "create usage limits" reservation. It is the only clause in the
     category that gives a provider the contractual right to meter what it markets.
  3. Section 6's automation test is a rate limit written as a contractual term. It is what lets us
     act against a script without reclassifying a heavy human as an abuser, which the ASA
     expressly forbids ("exceeding a particular usage level ... will not in itself render a user
     illegitimate").

  NO PRICES ON THIS PAGE. Prices are per-territory and move; the in-app paywall is the only
