  <h2>Who you are contracting with</h2>
  <p>Vocele is operated by <strong>Yauheni Malashchytski, trading as OverX AI</strong> (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;), an individual trader. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:support@vocele.app">support@vocele.app</a>.</p>

  <h2>Accepting these terms</h2>
  <p>These terms apply to the Vocele app and this website. By creating an account or using Vocele you accept them. If you do not accept them, do not use Vocele. If you are using Vocele on behalf of someone else, you confirm you are allowed to accept these terms for them.</p>

  <h2>Who can use Vocele</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 13 years old. In the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom you must be at least 16, unless the law of your country sets a lower age for consenting to online services, in which case that age applies. If you are under 18, you may use Vocele only with the involvement of a parent or guardian, who accepts these terms with you. We may close an account if we learn it belongs to someone below these ages.</p>

  <h2>Plans and what each one includes</h2>
  <p>Spoken conversation with the AI coach and pronunciation scoring are <strong>metered</strong>: each paid plan includes a stated number of conversation minutes and pronunciation checks. The exact numbers for your plan are shown on the purchase screen in the app, before you pay, and are listed on our <a href="/fair-use">Usage &amp; Fair Use</a> page. They are part of these terms.</p>
  <p>Everything else — word sets, stories, reviews, grammar, your vocabulary and your progress — is included in your plan and does not consume conversation minutes. Any storage limit on saved vocabulary is stated in the same places.</p>
  <p>A monthly plan&rsquo;s allowance arrives when you subscribe and at each renewal. A weekly plan spreads the same monthly amounts across a cycle, weighted towards the first week; an annual plan grants its twelve months together. Unused minutes carry over and are not swept, but the balance you may hold at once is capped: two months&rsquo; worth on a monthly or weekly plan, and on an annual plan the twelve months you bought.</p>

  <h2>Reaching your limit, and our right to set limits</h2>
  <p>When you have used the conversation minutes included in your plan, the exercise you are in the middle of finishes — we do not cut you off mid-sentence — and new spoken exercises pause until your next instalment arrives. The app tells you when that is. Everything unmetered stays available. You can move to a larger plan at any time; you are never required to, and nothing is charged automatically because you ran out.</p>
  <p>We may change, suspend or discontinue any part of the service, and <strong>we may set or change usage limits for the service</strong>, including the allowances described above. If we reduce an allowance included in a plan you have already paid for, we will tell you at least 30 days beforehand and the change will not take effect until your next renewal, so you can cancel first. We will not reduce it during a period you have already paid for.</p>
  <p>We may also apply short-term technical limits — queuing or rate-limiting requests — where that is necessary to keep the service working for everyone or to protect it from abuse.</p>

