  <h2>Price, billing and renewal</h2>
  <p>Paid plans are sold as auto-renewing subscriptions through Apple&rsquo;s App Store. The price, the billing period and what the plan includes are shown to you on the purchase screen before you pay, in your local currency including any applicable tax.</p>
  <p>Your subscription <strong>renews automatically</strong> at the end of each period at the then-current price, and Apple charges your Apple Account, until you cancel. Apple takes the renewal within 24 hours before the period ends. All billing for in-app purchases is handled by Apple under Apple&rsquo;s terms, not by us.</p>
  <p>If we change the price of a plan you are subscribed to, Apple will ask you to confirm the new price before it takes effect; if you do not confirm, the subscription does not renew.</p>

  <h2>Free trials and introductory offers</h2>
  <p>Where we offer a free trial or an introductory price, its length and what follows it are shown on the purchase screen. <strong>Unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends, it converts to a paid subscription and Apple charges you at the price shown.</strong> Trials are limited to one per person and per Apple Account, and we may change or withdraw an offer at any time before you accept it.</p>

  <h2>Cancelling</h2>
  <p>You can cancel at any time in your Apple Account subscription settings, up to 24 hours before the next renewal. Cancelling stops future renewals; your plan keeps working until the end of the period you have already paid for. Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription.</p>
  <p>You can delete your account, and everything in it, in the app under Settings &rarr; Account &rarr; Delete account. Deleting your account does not cancel your Apple subscription — cancel that separately.</p>

